WEBVTT

00:00:00.106 --> 00:00:01.417
The payment is shielded.

00:00:01.705 --> 00:00:03.498
The extra lookup still leaks.

00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:07.271
Across three checks, ten calls, and

00:00:07.347 --> 00:00:10.310
three candidate transactions: three findings

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.362
before the fixes.

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:12.503
Zero after.

00:00:13.153 --> 00:00:15.565
For A1, start with GetBlockRange.

00:00:15.854 --> 00:00:17.522
Both runs scan the same window.

00:00:17.811 --> 00:00:19.439
Now look at GetTransaction on the

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:19.940
left.

00:00:20.241 --> 00:00:22.003
The payment appears twice.

00:00:22.281 --> 00:00:24.987
On the right, each candidate gets one
lookup.

00:00:25.646 --> 00:00:27.456
That extra question is the leak.

00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:33.123
The extra lookup tells this server

00:00:33.123 --> 00:00:34.644
that the session is interested in

00:00:34.644 --> 00:00:35.593
that transaction.

00:00:35.882 --> 00:00:37.374
That's the limit of the claim.

00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:39.402
It doesn't identify the recipient.

00:00:40.346 --> 00:00:42.451
The fixed trace keeps GetBlockRange.

00:00:42.752 --> 00:00:44.627
For the memo, it fetches all

00:00:44.627 --> 00:00:47.333
three candidates once, in chain order.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.503
The extra GetTransaction is gone.

00:00:50.138 --> 00:00:52.809
That's the request I'd want CI to catch.

00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:02.503
A3 is app.log.

00:01:02.792 --> 00:01:04.738
The left side contains the decrypted

00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:06.442
memo and the address.

00:01:06.719 --> 00:01:08.394
My app wrote a plaintext copy

00:01:08.394 --> 00:01:09.213
into its log.

00:01:09.491 --> 00:01:10.864
That's a copy I didn't need.

00:01:11.775 --> 00:01:13.426
On the right, those fields say

00:01:13.426 --> 00:01:14.127
redacted.

00:01:14.416 --> 00:01:15.212
Same payment.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.214
Same check.

00:01:16.492 --> 00:01:18.243
Less private data in the log.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.035
That's a change I can actually review.

00:01:24.094 --> 00:01:24.572
A2.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.081
Here's SendTransaction.

00:01:26.347 --> 00:01:28.481
Unsigned transparent test bytes on the

00:01:28.481 --> 00:01:28.982
left.

00:01:29.271 --> 00:01:31.482
The fixed run refuses the send.

00:01:31.771 --> 00:01:32.697
No funds move.

00:01:34.092 --> 00:01:35.146
This is a staged chain.

00:01:35.413 --> 00:01:37.490
Darkside doesn't check consensus.

00:01:38.224 --> 00:01:39.890
I'm checking this server's view and

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.151
these application logs.

00:01:41.418 --> 00:01:44.150
The leaky run shows three findings.

00:01:44.441 --> 00:01:46.023
The fixed run shows none.

00:01:46.279 --> 00:01:48.528
Other privacy leaks can still exist.

00:01:49.094 --> 00:01:50.680
make demo reruns the checks.

00:01:50.969 --> 00:01:53.045
The successful CI run and raw

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:54.466
traces are linked here.

00:01:54.743 --> 00:01:57.060
I'd check those before trusting the green
result.
